From: At30c <173511395+At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m21s: wait for TZTS before restarting Keymaster

TEEgris becoming ready only confirms the base secure-world transport.  The
legacy F415F Keymaster service also needs the TZTS auxiliary daemon and ACSD
path before it can open the SKeymaster trusted application.  Restarting it on
vendor.tzdaemon=Ready races that setup and leaves Keystore2 blocked forever.

Keep starting TZTS when TEEgris is ready, but defer both service restarts until
vendor.tzts_daemon=Ready confirms that the auxiliary path is available.

--- a/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
+++ b/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
@@ -21,10 +21,10 @@ on property:vendor.tzdaemon=Ready
     setprop vendor.TEEGRIS.loaded true
     write /proc/iccc_ready 1
     start tzts_service
-    restart vendor.keymaster-4-0
-    restart keystore2
 
 on property:vendor.tzts_daemon=Ready
+    restart vendor.keymaster-4-0
+    restart keystore2
 
 on post-fs-data
 # TEEGRIS service
